{"name":"Farmhouse Red","hex":"#a34b41","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"farmhouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A house (usually the main house) on a farm; thus:\n A farmer's residence.\n\nA house that was once a farmer's residence albeit today lived in by residents whose occupation is not farming.","A farmer's residence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farmhouse"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Farmhouse","blocks":[{"text":"A farmhouse is a building that serves as the primary quarters in a rural or agricultural setting. Historically, farmhouses were often combined with space for animals called a housebarn. Other farmhouses may be connected to one or more barns, built to form a courtyard, or with each farm building separate from each other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Einsiedeln_IMG_2819.JPG/330px-Einsiedeln_IMG_2819.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farmhouse","wikidata":"Q489357"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/500px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/1280px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/500px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Devil's Farmhouse in Mellieħa, Malta, built by the Order of St. John with limestone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Devil's_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg/250px-Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg/500px-Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg/250px-Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser